comments.message:
Please avoid using the `_p` msgbuf APIs, they only exist to cater to old library APIs where message fields were passed as individual pointer parameters. That's not the case here, we can access the lvalue via the struct member. This should be rewritten as:

```
pldm_msgbuf_extract(buf, req->effecter_id);
pldm_msgbuf_extract(buf, req->effecter_operational_state);
```

Perhaps:
```suggestion
	switch (req->effecter_operational_state) {
	case EFFECTER_OPER_STATE_ENABLED_UPDATEPENDING:
	case EFFECTER_OPER_STATE_ENABLED_NOUPDATEPENDING:
	case EFFECTER_OPER_STATE_DISABLED:
	case EFFECTER_OPER_STATE_UNAVAILABLE:
		break;
	default:
		return -EINVAL;
	}
```

You must add a test of the result here because you use the value of `operational_state` below.

```suggestion
	rc = pldm_msgbuf_extract(buf, operational_state);
	if (rc) {
		return pldm_msgbuf_discard(buf, rc);
	}

```

The result test can only be omitted for extracted values that aren't later used.
